    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνοπλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπλον</span> or <i>large shield,</i> of
			the Persians, who bore only <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέρρα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.62
			</span></i>: generally, <i>unarmed,</i> Pl<i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				299b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				42.17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἄ.,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὁπλιτικόν,</span> of citizens <i>not
				entrusted with arms,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1289b32
			</span></i>:—of ships, <i>unarmed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.12.3
			</span></i>. (On the form 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄοπλος.</span>
			)</div>
